From: Nestor Monroy <46802445+NestorMonroy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:37:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Let a declared policy forbid the claude-cli fallback

recommendExecution always fell back to claude-cli when no local model
qualified, and the pool asked for that fallback itself when the
managed Ollama did not start. Choosing a provider nobody authorized
belongs to neither of them silently.

An ExecutionPolicy now declares the allowed runtimes and the ones the
control plane measured down. Without an allowed runtime that has a
candidate the recommender throws NoCandidateError (no_candidate or
runtime_unavailable) instead of returning claude-cli. The open policy
keeps today's behavior. agent-recommend takes --allow-runtime and
--unavailable, repeatable, and refuses --runtime claude-cli outside
the declared policy.

Annulment: forcing the provider branch to be usable drops exactly the
three fail-closed cases (8 pass, 3 fail).

Refs: TASK-THYROX-0743
